# Rank 1632 / CVE-2024-2221 (GHSA-hm95-xqg2-4w57, CWE-22): qdrant's full
# snapshot REST API served and deleted files at a request-chosen path.
#
# GET and DELETE /snapshots/{snapshot_name} hand the URL segment straight to
# get_full_snapshot_path in lib/storage/src/content_manager/snapshots/mod.rs,
# which builds the path with `Path::new(toc.snapshots_path()).join(snapshot_name)`
# and returns it after an existence check alone -- no canonicalisation, no
# containment, so `../` in the segment reaches any file the process can read or
# remove. The sibling Collection::get_snapshot_path in
# lib/collection/src/collection/snapshots.rs canonicalised both sides and
# compared them, but joined onto the raw directory and returned the
# non-canonicalised path. The fixed revision (3ab5172e, "Fix arbitrary path traversal
# vulnerability in full snapshot REST API (#3856)", first released in v1.8.3)
# canonicalises the directory first, joins onto the canonical directory,
# canonicalises the result, and rejects anything whose components do not start
# with the canonical directory.
#
# Corpus corrections. The pool row's commit e6411907 is "Bump version to 1.8.0
# (#3779)" -- a release bump touching Cargo.toml, a changelog and
# docs/redoc/default_version.js, which is also where the recorded `javascript`
# language most plausibly comes from. The advisory itself references that bump,
# so the row faithfully records a wrong advisory reference. The fixing commit is Rust,
# landing in lib/storage and lib/collection.
#
# ATTENTION, engine gap: the Rust frontend emits no nir.Return, so a function's
# return value never carries taint to its callers. Loweringady flows a
# `nir.Return` value into the function's `__ret__` node
# (internal/extract/lowering/lowering.go, the nir.Return case), and the Go
# frontend feeds it (internal/extract/frontend/golang/golang.go returns
# nir.Return for result statements), but internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/rust.go
# constructs no Return statement at all -- blockTail exists for if/else
# expression bodies only. Measured with a minimal pair in one file:
#
#   helper computes `Path::new(dir).join(name)` and the caller reads the file
#   -> VYQL-PATH-001 (the join is an untraced method call, so its result keeps
#      the argument taint while the flow stays inside one function);
#   the identical join moved into a helper that returns the joined path
#   -> nothing. Not the join's fault: a helper that returns its parameter
#   unchanged, or `name.to_string()`, is equally dark, while the same three
#   shapes in Go all report. The taint dies at the callee boundary because no
#   return node exists to flow into `__ret__`.
#
# On the real tree this is the whole story of the vulnerable endpoint:
# src/actix/api/snapshot_api.rs get_full_snapshot labels the `web::Path`
# parameter as code.HttpInput, taint flows through do_get_full_snapshot into
# get_full_snapshot_path's parameter and reaches the join, and stops there --
# the path that comes back and is opened is clean. Naming the sink does not
# help: binding `actix_files::NamedFile::open` as code.FilePathAccess is
# measured on both revisions of the real tree and adds exactly two findings
# (snapshot_api.rs:134 and :449, fed through unresolvable method receivers,
# which do pass argument taint through conservatively), identical before and
# at the fixed revision, so the binding discriminates nothing and is not shipped.
#
# The remediation would also be invisible at the caller-side sink even with
# return flow, because the containment check lives inside the callee -- the
# Rust attribution gap recorded at rank 1364 -- and Rust has no live
# canonicalisation control at all: pathCanonicalization23 in
# vyql/bindings/packages/rust/m222602a5.vyql is gated on
# `dependency("std::fs")`, which no Cargo.toml ever satisfies.
#
# The expect block keeps the source, the join and the sink of the real
# endpoint (with std::fs::read_to_string standing in for the actix-files sink,
# which no binding labels) in one function, where the flow works. The first
# reject block moves the join behind a function boundary -- the shape of the
# real code -- and pins the miss: it reports nothing today and starts
# reporting once return-value taint exists. The second reject block is the
# patched form.

test "rank1632: a request-chosen snapshot name is joined and opened in one function"
  lang rust
  expect VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  use actix_files::NamedFile;
  use actix_web::web;
  use std::path::Path;

  pub async fn do_get_full_snapshot(snapshots_path: &str, snapshot_name: &str) -> std::io::Result<String> {
      let file_name = Path::new(snapshots_path).join(snapshot_name);
      std::fs::read_to_string(file_name)
  }

  #[get("/snapshots/{snapshot_name}")]
  async fn get_full_snapshot(toc: web::Data<TableOfContent>, path: web::Path<String>) -> impl Responder {
      let snapshot_name = path.into_inner();
      do_get_full_snapshot(toc.snapshots_path(), &snapshot_name).await
  }
  ```

test "rank1632: the same join returned from a helper and opened by the caller reports nothing"
  lang rust
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  use actix_web::web;
  use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};

  pub async fn get_full_snapshot_path(snapshots_path: &str, snapshot_name: &str) -> PathBuf {
      Path::new(snapshots_path).join(snapshot_name)
  }

  pub async fn do_get_full_snapshot(snapshots_path: &str, snapshot_name: &str) -> std::io::Result<String> {
      let file_name = get_full_snapshot_path(snapshots_path, snapshot_name).await;
      std::fs::read_to_string(file_name)
  }

  #[get("/snapshots/{snapshot_name}")]
  async fn get_full_snapshot(toc: web::Data<TableOfContent>, path: web::Path<String>) -> impl Responder {
      let snapshot_name = path.into_inner();
      do_get_full_snapshot(toc.snapshots_path(), &snapshot_name).await
  }
  ```

test "rank1632: the snapshot path canonicalised and contained inside the snapshots directory"
  lang rust
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  use actix_web::web;
  use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};

  pub async fn get_full_snapshot_path(snapshots_path: &str, snapshot_name: &str) -> std::io::Result<PathBuf> {
      let absolute_snapshot_dir = match Path::new(snapshots_path).canonicalize() {
          Ok(p) => p,
          Err(_) => return Err(std::io::Error::new(std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound, "snapshot dir")),
      };
      let absolute_snapshot_path = match absolute_snapshot_dir.join(snapshot_name).canonicalize() {
          Ok(p) => p,
          Err(_) => return Err(std::io::Error::new(std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound, "snapshot")),
      };
      if !absolute_snapshot_path.starts_with(&absolute_snapshot_dir) {
          return Err(std::io::Error::new(std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound, "snapshot"));
      }
      Ok(absolute_snapshot_path)
  }

  pub async fn do_get_full_snapshot(snapshots_path: &str, snapshot_name: &str) -> std::io::Result<String> {
      let file_name = get_full_snapshot_path(snapshots_path, snapshot_name).await?;
      std::fs::read_to_string(file_name)
  }

  #[get("/snapshots/{snapshot_name}")]
  async fn get_full_snapshot(toc: web::Data<TableOfContent>, path: web::Path<String>) -> impl Responder {
      let snapshot_name = path.into_inner();
      do_get_full_snapshot(toc.snapshots_path(), &snapshot_name).await
  }
  ```
